{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1130371-w20-docile-and-ragabash","id":1130371,"title":"[W20] Docile and Ragabash","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-17T11:34:03-07:00","id":1130371,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> [W20] Docile and Ragabash","content":"How does the Docile Flaw work with Ragabash with only one Rage?<br /> <br /> <b>Docile (1 to 3 point Flaw)</b><br /> Your distance from &quot;the wolf&quot; hampers the fires of Rage within you. For every point of Docile you take, your Maximum Rage is lower by 2 and can never be bought above that level. Other may see you as &quot;domesticated&quot; or &quot;more dog than wolf&quot; and react with derision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T17:55:41-07:00","id":1130625,"title":"","content":"I think it only lowers the ceiling. You wouldn't have any auspices actually lose Rage from their base starting values unless you were an Ahroun that took it as a 3 point flaw, at which point you would have a Rage of 4 instead of 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T19:47:16-07:00","id":1130657,"title":"","content":"Apparently I had it wrong on my old character. Thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T20:21:35-07:00","id":1130675,"title":"","content":"Something I'd been wondering for a bit? Would a Ragabash be the Garou most likely to live as a &quot;Traditional&quot; housewife on the surface, as trying to pretend to be such a thing would be a challenge, balancing it with ones duties to Gaia<br /> <br /> and shows an element of peversity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T00:35:39-07:00","id":1130737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1130371-w20-docile-and-ragabash?p=1130675#post1130675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I'd been wondering for a bit? Would a Ragabash be the Garou most likely to live as a &quot;Traditional&quot; housewife on the surface, as trying to pretend to be such a thing would be a challenge, balancing it with ones duties to Gaia<br /> <br /> and shows an element of peversity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt that there's any particular splat more likely to do so. There are some substantially less likely to do so. The number of either who do are going to be few among a people who are already thinned out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T11:20:23-07:00","id":1130901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1130371-w20-docile-and-ragabash?p=1130675#post1130675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a Ragabash be the Garou most likely to live as a &quot;Traditional&quot; housewife on the surface, as trying to pretend to be such a thing would be a challenge, balancing it with ones duties to Gaia</div> </div> </div> </div>Ragabash, since they start with only one Rage, can more easily deal with human society since the Curse affects them minimally. So yes, if one wanted to live as a traditional housewife (or any other role among the Flock) they could do so.<br /> <br /> Garou with higher Rage could also attempt to do so, but they would have increasing difficulty. Even someone with just two Rage (a starting Theurge or a Ragabash who has increased Rage) will have trouble with the Curse 10% of the time. However, if their immediate friends and family have high Willpower, and they keep to themselves and avoid social situations, even higher Rage Garou could make it work.<br /> <br /> At Rage four however, any Garou starts putting their family at risk as they could conceivably make a Rage roll and frenzy. Since Rage rolls can come anytime there is strong emotion (like lust or passion), even a rather ordinary life could result in a terrible incident.<br /> <br /> Now outside of Curse mechanics, a Ragabash as questioner of the ways has more leeway in her behavior. Less specific auspice expectations, and since any Renown works, fewer penalties to advancing in rank. But that only impacts the werewolf if they really want to be involved in Garou society. Assuming this isn't meant to be some kind of ruse, a werewolf who wants to continue in that kind of role strikes as someone who is either Ronin or a Reluctant Garou who is actually opting out of Garou society.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T14:11:34-07:00","id":1131436,"title":"","content":"Something Ive been wondering for a bit? Think rage gnosis and Willpower will stop varying by breed and auspice in 4th edition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T17:53:32-07:00","id":1131532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1130371-w20-docile-and-ragabash?p=1131436#post1131436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something Ive been wondering for a bit? Think rage gnosis and Willpower will stop varying by breed and auspice in 4th edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's going to be marketed as a 5th edition, and even V5 has barely enough details out to tell anything about it yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}